      "writtenOn": "2025-10-28T21:08:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I hadn\u0027t realized that the behaviour on Windows for loading DXC had changed like that. So I just assumed that Windows would be able to pick up the system one if needed.\n\nIf that is not a desired use case, then I probably can generalize this to not be behind the is linux check, and make it a FATAL similar how to turning on IR_BINARY without PROTOBUF is.\n\n(My original issue was that I only turned on the TINT flag when initially setting up my Linux dev env, and got a linking error at the end of the build about missing dxc, and was wanting to put something during the configuration stage in CMake to warn me about missing the DXC flag. To my knowledge GN works fine, my fuzzer builds in GN didn\u0027t have the same linking issue, but I didn\u0027t explcitily turn on dxc, so I assume there is logic handling that)",
